ProbabilityTheory.Kernel.rdist_symm.statement:
Let $T$, $T'$ and $G$ be countable with measurable singletons ($G$ an abelian group). Let $\kappa$ be a finite kernel from $T$ to $G$ and $\eta$ a finite kernel from $T'$ to $G$, and let $\mu$ on $T$ and $
u$ on $T'$ be probability measures with finite support. Then the kernel Ruzsa distance is symmetric: $d_k[\kappa;\mu \,\#\, \eta;
u] = d_k[\eta;
u \,\#\, \kappa;\mu]$.
